─ hint ─────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────────
 run-wrapper.command (list, required): The server's command and arguments (exec form: ["/server/srv", "-port", "2456"])                                         
 No shell expansion: flk-run runs it as is. For arguments built from the environment, use ["bash", "-c", "exec ./srv -name \"$NAME\""] or write them in a       
 prestart hook.                                                                                                                                                 
 A list: a, b, c (or a TOML array for items with commas).                                                                                                       
 Runs the server under flk-run, a supervisor shared by every app that uses this snippet, and wires up how it stops.                                             
